# UNIVERSAL PATTERN
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

META_PRINCIPLE:
  name: "Exhaustive Enumeration → Complete Primitive Sets"
  
  pattern: |
    For any domain with:
      1. Discrete, well-defined input space
      2. Exhaustively enumerable configurations
      3. Mutually-exclusive, complete output set
      4. Mathematical or empirical provability
    
    Then:
      → A finite, irreducible set of primitives exists
      → The set size depends on input dimensionality
      → Typically 13-26 primitives per domain
      → Each primitive is atomic and indivisible
  
  evidence:
    - Boolean: 2² input → 16 functions
    - Temporal: 3 x 3 input → 13 relations
    - Spatial: 3 x 3 x 3 input → 26 relations
    - Causal: 2⁴ input → 16 types
    - Others: All follow pattern

  implication: |
    The universe doesn't construct primitive sets arbitrarily.
    They emerge necessarily from mathematical exhaustion.
    This applies to:
      ✓ Physics (particles, forces)
      ✓ Chemistry (bonding types)
      ✓ Biology (genetic mechanisms)
      ✓ Cognition (mental operations)
      ✓ Everything with finite input space

